{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Sabbamitta","html":"<article id='thag2.15'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 2.15 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 2.15 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dukanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Twos </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dutiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Two </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sabbamittattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sabbamitta </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Jano janamhi sambaddho, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>People are attached to people; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>janamevassito jano; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>people depend on people; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Jano janena heṭhīyati, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>people are hurt by people; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>heṭheti ca jano janaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and people hurt people. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ko hi tassa janenattho, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>So what’s the point of people, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>janena janitena vā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>or those born of people? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Janaṁ ohāya gacchaṁ taṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Go, abandon these people, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>heṭhayitvā bahuṁ janan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who’ve hurt so many people. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Sabbamitto thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
